Accept an inotifyd mask of only x on Windows.
The x event had no notification filter of its own, so a mask of only x
gave an empty filter and was rejected as invalid, though watching only
for the end of a directory is a reasonable request. The end of a watch
is reported whatever the filter, so give x the directory name filter,
which rarely fires; the changes it lets through are not reported, since
x is the only event selected.

---
 miscutils/inotifyd.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/miscutils/inotifyd.c
+++ b/miscutils/inotifyd.c
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@
 };
 
 static const unsigned mask_values[] = {
-	0x000,	// File is no longer watched (usually deleted)
+	0x002,	// File is no longer watched (any nonzero filter will do)
 	0x003,	// Subfile was created
 	0x003,	// Subfile was deleted
 	0x1fc,	// File was modified (everything except create/delete/move)
